{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31007 - PROTEIN:5802",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which isorhamnetin 3-O-2''-glucosylrhamnoside influences Hs746T through a series of target interactions. The drug is implicated in targeting Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is subsequently targeted by Neridienone A and Ginsenoside R10, both of which are linked to Hs746T. This indicates a possible pathway where isorhamnetin 3-O-2''-glucosylrhamnoside may act as a modulator of the signaling cascade initiated by these compounds, potentially through enzyme inhibition or regulatory interactions. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of isorhamnetin 3-O-2''-glucosylrhamnoside in the regulation of Hs746T.",
